mode profile-free
  extract.builtin_profile = phi 1; profile "kz-static-builtin-minimal"; (profile hash in the header)
  extract.profile = kz-static-builtin-minimal / 
  extract.p0_table = P0 table revision 2 (2026-10-30), 72 entries
  extract.p0_table_scope = families listed whole: thread creation, mutex and spin lock, semaphore, condition variable, sleep, termination of the calling thread or process, thread identity, thread-specific data, cleanup handlers, dynamic loading (open and symbol lookup), data functions; with the ISO C11 <threads.h> members of those families and the glibc 2.39 *_clock* members.  Not in this revision: read-write locks (pthread_rwlock_*; their shared acquisitions are not read by the lock-set analysis, so the family is left out whole and its acquisitions are no lock operations), barriers (pthread_barrier_*), one-time initialization (pthread_once, call_once), thread cancellation of another thread (pthread_cancel and the cancellation state functions), signals (kill, raise, pthread_kill, sigwait), dlclose, dlerror and dladdr, and functions a compiler or a fortify wrapper calls without a call in the source (__stack_chk_fail, __chk_fail and the *_chk functions)
  extract.derivation_rules = wrapper derivation rules F7/F8 revision 1 (2026-10-30)
  extract.targets_rule = R-T1,R-T2 (target rules revision 1): the targets of the second pass, chosen from the first pass's ARGFLOW (R-T1) and READS with RETURNS (R-T2), shared bases only (a global object, a global array element, the pointee of a global pointer or of a pointer field reached from a global)
